[h1]No Limit Timer Sensor[/h1]

Make maximum timer limit configurable duration beyond the default 600 seconds, or 10 cycles.

[h2]Recommend Mod[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/id=2904048344]Configurable Timers[/url] - With this mod, you can adjust current counting time
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/id=2277619848]No Sensor Limits[/url] - Might override "maximum cycles" but not "maximum seconds"
[/list]

[h2]Well Known Issue[/h2]
[list]
[*]In-game simulation effectively does timeElapsedInCurrentState += 1/30. As that value grows, the float step gets coarser. Above 1,048,576 s (~1,748 cycles), adding 1/30 can round to zero, so the timer can effectively freeze.
[*]Even before that, drift is significant: simulating the game's float addition gives +95(late 0.32%) s at 30,000 s, -269(early 0.67%) s at 40,000 s, and -1,306 s (2.2% early) at 60,000 s. 
[*]It is recommended to keep timer settings under 60,000 seconds(or 10 100 cycles) to ensure accurate counting.
[/list]

